00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.517
-Okay. Really?

00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:01.019
-But he saw
the size of the rats,

00:02:01.019 --> 00:02:03.690
and he was disgusted,

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.625
so he just jumped in an Uber
and came on back uptown.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.026
-He did? Oh.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.829
Oh, well, that's nice.
I'm glad that he's back.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.030
I'm glad that he's back.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.231
You haven't --
You were on the West Coast.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:13.432
You've been doing
a lot of traveling.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:15.534
-Yeah, been doing traveling.
I love it.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.436
-You love being on the road?
-Having a bunch of fun.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:18.604
I love being on the road.
You know?

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.707
Stand up is my foundation.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.075
-So I love being -- going --
me and my cousin.

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:25.344
My cousin is with me, Lavelle.
He's with me.

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.847
His name is Lavelle,
but his real name is Anthony.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.549
-Okay.
-I call him by his --

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.719
I don't call him by
his "government."

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:36.689
He calls his real name
his "government."

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.325
So we go through the airport.
You know, the TSA.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.060
-Yeah.
-Security.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.362
And when you stay
on the yellow line

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:45.030
and you got to put
your hands up like this.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.132
-Yep.
-My cousin said,

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.767
"Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I know the position.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.702
I've been doing this
since I was 14."

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.305
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.006
-Now, it's very confusing.
If somebody

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.874
